Pattern 1: DELETE + INSERT (simple, transactional)
BEGIN;
DELETE FROM target WHERE partition_date = '2024-01-01';
INSERT INTO target SELECT ... FROM source WHERE date = '2024-01-01';
COMMIT;

Pattern 2: INSERT ... ON CONFLICT (upsert)
INSERT INTO target (...) VALUES (...)
ON CONFLICT (primary_key) DO UPDATE SET col = EXCLUDED.col;

Pattern 3: MERGE (PostgreSQL 15+)
MERGE INTO target t
USING source s ON t.id = s.id
WHEN MATCHED THEN UPDATE SET ...
WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT ...;

Pattern 4: Temp table + INSERT ... ON CONFLICT
CREATE TEMP TABLE staging (LIKE target);
COPY staging FROM 'file.csv';
INSERT INTO target SELECT * FROM staging ON CONFLICT ...;
DROP TABLE staging;

Nubank preference: likely Pattern 2 or 4 for daily batch loads.

